      "**Allergic rhinitis** is IgE-mediated nasal inflammation (itch, sneeze, watery discharge, blockage) graded by **ARIA into intermittent or persistent and mild or moderate-severe**, and treated with allergen avoidance, saline and a correctly aimed **intranasal corticosteroid** (plus a non-sedating antihistamine or azelastine); **acute rhinosinusitis** is viral in over 98%, and an antibiotic (amoxicillin or co-amoxiclav) is justified only with **symptoms beyond 10 days, double sickening or severe onset with fever over 39 C and purulent discharge**, while **orbital cellulitis, intracranial spread, mucormycosis and any unilateral nasal sign** must never be missed.",
